 melds are Pungs. So All Chows is not applicable. The user has three Pungs and one Chi. So the hand is four melds (two Pungs, one Chi, one Chi) and a pair. The pair is T4. The scoring would be based on the patterns. Since the user has multiple Pungs (three of them), and a Chi, maybe they can get points for All Pungs (4 points) or other patterns. But the main thing is to complete the hand. So discarding W3 allows them to form the necessary melds.\n\nAlternatively, if they discard T4, they have W3, B2, B3, B4. Form Chi of B2-B3-B4, and then need a pair. The pair could be W3 if they get another. But there are 3 W3s left. So that's possible. But if they discard T4, they lose the chance to have a pair of T4. So maybe discarding W3 is better because they can form a pair of T4 immediately.\n\nWait, the user's hand after discarding W3 would have T4 as a single tile. If they can get another T4, they can form a pair. But if they discard T4, then they have W3 as a single tile, needing another W3. So which is more likely? The unshown T4s are 2 left, and W3s are 3 left. So W3 is more available. But the user already has a T4 in the meld. If they discard the T4 in their hand, they still have one in the meld. So they can't form a pair of T4. Wait, the pair requires two of the same tile. The T4 in the meld is part of the Chi, so they have one T4 in the meld and one in the hand. If they discard the hand's T4, they have one T4 in the meld. That's only one tile, so they can't form a pair. Therefore, if they discard T4, the pair would need to be W3. If they discard W3, they have the T4 in hand (one) and the T4 in the meld (one), making two T4s. So they can form a pair of T4. That's better because they can immediately form the pair without needing to draw another tile.\n\nTherefore, the best move is to discard W3. This allows them to form the fourth Chi (B2-B3-B4) and the pair of T4 (since they have two T4s: one in the meld and one in the hand). This would complete their hand. The other options would require drawing another tile for the pair, which is less certain.\n\nSo the answer is to play W3.\n", "output": "Evaluation: [Discarding W3 allows forming a Chi of B2-B3-B4 and a pair of T4, completing the hand with four melds and a pair. Other options require drawing tiles for the pair, which is less certain.]\nReason: [By discarding W3, the hand can form a Chi of B2-B3-B4 (using existing B2, B3, B4) and a pair of T4 (one in hand and one in the existing Chi meld). This completes the winning hand structure immediately. Other options like discarding B2 or B4 would require drawing specific tiles (B5 or B3) to form the necessary melds and pair, which is riskier given limited unshown tiles.]\nAnswer: Play W3"}
